# `cd e2e_playwright && honcho start` boots everything AND runs the suite:
# honcho starts all three processes; when `tests` finishes it tears the others
# down and exits with pytest's status. (`honcho run <cmd>` is one-off only.)
#
# Redis runs on a non-default port with persistence off, so a developer's own
# redis-server and its data are left alone. The app needs it at startup:
# dramatiq connects while the Flask app is being built.
redis: redis-server --port ${E2E_REDIS_PORT:-6399} --save '' --dir ${E2E_DIR:-/tmp/abilian-sbe-e2e}
web: sh serve.sh
tests: sh run_tests.sh
